==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilegeMatrix  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_LeastPrivilegeMatrix.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets Alloy invent a Permitted access whose (role, kind) pair is not in PermMatrix.Allowed; the injection forces an administrator-on-record-lookup Permitted attempt — a textbook least-privilege violation.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_017_AdminEndpointRoleOnly, FR_005_AdminNoClinicalAccess
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_017_AdminEndpointRoleOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_005_AdminNoClinicalAccess: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: clearing the gating fact lets a clinical-role caller obtain Permitted access without any matching active CareTeamMembership; the injection forces such a counterexample to exist within scope.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_CareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: without this fact Alloy can produce a clinical access attempt with zero AuditEntry atoms pointing at it; the injection guarantees at least one such attempt exists.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_OneAuditPerAttempt
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_OneAuditPerAttempt: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttributionCorrect  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditAttributionCorrect.als
    rationale: removing attribution coupling lets the recordedUser/role/kind/outcome diverge from the underlying attempt; the injection forces a mismatched audit entry into the universe.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_013_AuditAttribution
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditAttribution: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAppendOnly  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditAppendOnly.als
    rationale: clearing the append-only fact allows AuditAction atoms whose op is ModifyOp or DeleteOp; the injection forces a Modify-op audit action, which is exactly the immutability violation the assertion catches.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_014_AuditImmutable
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NotesAppendOnly  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_NotesAppendOnly.als
    rationale: clearing notes append-only enforcement lets the universe include a ModifyOp NoteAction; the injection forces one to exist, violating FR-011.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_011_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AdminNoClinicalContent  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AdminNoClinicalContent.als
    rationale: removing the content-blindness fact lets an AdminResponse atom set containsClinicalContent = TrueB; the injection forces such a leak to exist, exactly the FR-018 violation.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_018_AdminNoClinicalContent
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AdminNoClinicalContent: FAIL (expected)

